      'Stucco vs brick is one of the most common debates among San Antonio homeowners planning a new build, a remodel, or a re-siding project. Both materials are well-suited to the South Texas climate, both look right at home on San Antonio architecture, and both last far longer than vinyl or fiber cement. But they differ significantly in upfront cost, long-term maintenance, design flexibility, and practical performance — and those differences matter when you are writing the check.',
      '## Upfront Installation Cost',
